Base : lettre de Matthieu adaptée pour Houdini Generalist. Précision ajoutée sur la double candidature avec l'offre TA Stylised Environments. Objet : Houdini Artist. (7 October 2026)

## English (7 October 2026)

Subject: Houdini Artist

To the recruitment team,

Hello Ripple and Roll,

I am writing about your opening for Houdini Generalist. I also submitted an application for your "TA Stylised Environments" opening, as my day-to-day work sits right at the intersection of procedural technical art and Houdini generation.

"From SOPs to VOPs, you know your nodes, VEXing your way out of pretty much anything": this is what I spend my days doing. Whether it is building procedural assets from scratch, writing custom VEX setups, generating textures through Copernicus, or lighting and rendering in Karma and Unreal Engine, Houdini is my core tool.

My name is Matthieu Huguet, I am 25 and I work as a freelance Technical Artist and 3D Artist, based in Aix-en-Provence, France.

I studied a Game Design Bachelor at LISAA Paris, a Master's at ARTFX Montpellier, then technical art courses at Gnomon and through Harvard CS50, before going freelance in early 2025.

I worked on 2 NDA projects with Meerkat Studio and on an archviz project for a private client in Aix-en-Provence since 2025. All my work can be seen at matthieuhuguet.com.

Right now I am building procedural systems in Houdini that feed into realtime engines and offline renders alike. My latest published work: Fleur de Lys, Procedural Lily, Ceramic Tiles and HDA Stairs Component.

What I am looking for today is a mission with a team committed to an ambitious project. I need to work with experienced professionals and be part of a collective dynamic, something that working solo, however formative, cannot provide.

I am available to start right away, remotely, as a freelancer invoicing from France. My CV is attached, and I would be delighted to assist on whichever of the two roles best fits your current production needs.

I would be happy to talk with you by phone or video call, whenever suits you.

Matthieu Huguet
